<title>CANADA: TransGlobe sells IPC Intl shares.</title>
<headline>TransGlobe sells IPC Intl shares.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER, B.C. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransGlobe Energy Corp said it sold 750,000 of its Class A voting shares of IPC International Power Corp to SNC -- Lavalin Equity Inc, part of SNC-Lavalin Group Inc.</p>
<p>Shares were sold at a price of $1.35 per share for US$1.01 million, the company said.</p>
<p>TransGlobe said it had bought the shares for $1 per share.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
